	abstract = {Generative AI tools tend to be used as if they were built to gather or confirm truthful information, as if they were knowledge-based systems. As such, there is a discrepancy between how generative AI (e.g. ChatGPT) is conceived and used by the general public, and what it really is and can accomplish. Given a lack of proper legal framework and the widespread usage of these tools, organizations have raised red flags and urged academic institutions to reflect on governance principles for the use of generative AI. In this paper, we present the principles adopted by an Institutional AI committee to guide usage of generative AI, as well as the theoretical and practical considerations motivating their introduction. Copyright © 2025 by the authors.},
