	affiliations = {Banaras Hindu University, India},
	abstract = {The use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) creates new policy challenges regarding governance frameworks, application domains, economic impact, and other difficulties. When employing AI marketing, businesses must carefully balance customization against privacy, placing a high premium on protecting customer data. This can be achieved by implementing robust data protection protocols, providing clear privacy guidelines, and granting customers control over the data that is gathered about them. Ultimately, businesses ought to respect the rights of their customers and foster a sense of trust in their marketing plans. The current study helps interested marketers in developing a more grounded understanding of how AI can affect the lives of customers in good and bad ways. Also, an experimental case of Google is provided which will enable marketers and policy makers in better planning of AI ethical norms. With the help of a case study, this chapter fills a knowledge gap regarding AI marketing and advances the field by navigating the framework for ethical implementation of AI as adopted by Google AI. Given that AI marketing is a developing field, one major weakness in the literature on the subject is the lack of empirical studies analyzing the specifics of strategies in AI marketing. © 2025 Aliza and Asha Ram Tripathi. Published under exclusive licence by Emerald Publishing Limited. All rights reserved.},
