	abstract = {The rapid evolution of deepfake technology has created a paradox for businesses and policymakers. It offers groundbreaking opportunities while simultaneously posing significant ethical, security, and managerial challenges. As synthetic media and AI-driven content generation become more sophisticated, the need for strategic oversight, legal preparedness, and responsible implementation has never been greater. This book provides an in-depth analysis of how deepfake technology is reshaping industries, influencing consumer behaviour, and transforming managerial decision-making. This book explores the intersection of AI, blockchain, and deepfake technology, emphasising its role in business intelligence, cybersecurity, and financial risk management. It also highlights the legal complexities and ethical concerns surrounding deepfake misuse, particularly in digital identity fraud, misinformation campaigns, and economic crimes. Through real-world case studies and data-driven insights, this book examines deepfake technology's impact across diverse industries. In healthcare, deepfake-powered patient education tools enhance medical communication and engagement. In sports management, AI-generated simulations are revolutionising performance analytics and audience interaction. In the financial sector, deepfake risks pose new challenges in fraud detection and digital transaction security. This book also explores how synthetic media is influencing public trust in fiscal policies, consumer adoption of online travel platforms, and even religious tourism experiences. This book, with a special focus on the Indian regulatory landscape, dissects the legal, ethical, and societal implications of deepfake technology within a rapidly digitizing economy. It presents strategic frameworks for managers, business leaders, and policymakers to navigate the challenges posed by deepfake-driven cyber threats, AI misinformation, and data privacy concerns. The final section of the book offers practical solutions for businesses to mitigate deepfake risks, including AI-powered fraud prevention tools, blockchain-backed verification mechanisms, and corporate AI governance strategies. As organisations move toward a future where synthetic media blurs the lines between reality and manipulation, this book serves as a crucial guide for mastering managerial decision-making in the deepfake era. © 2025 by Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.},
