	abstract = {Generative Artificial Intelligence (AI) has rapidly become a powerful influence in modern technology, allowing machines to produce novel content that closely resembles human creativity. This chapter explores the ethical, privacy, and future implications of Generative AI and Large Language Models (LLMs). It outlines how biases emerge from training data, why transparency and accountability are essential, and how regulations strive to protect personal information. The text considers the social and cultural impacts of AI- generated content, examines workforce transformations due to automation and augmentation, and addresses the environmental costs of running large- scale models. It also highlights human- AI collaboration, the evolution of tools and policies for responsible AI, and the importance of integrating ethics at every step of technological development. Ultimately, it calls for thoughtful guidance and compassionate stewardship as Generative AI shapes the future of human creativity, knowledge, and interaction. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
