	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010750579?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This chapter explores the ethical implications of artificial intelligence (AI) in business, focusing on its role in greenwashing the practice of misleading consumers about environmental efforts. AI offers companies the tools to enhance efficiency, personalize services, and improve data analysis. However, without ethical frameworks and transparency, AI can also facilitate greenwashing by manipulating information to improve a company's image. This chapter reviews key ethical challenges, including privacy, accountability, and algorithmic biases. It also addresses how AI can support responsible business practices by enhancing transparency and monitoring sustainability efforts. A systematic literature review was conducted, identifying gaps in research on AI's dual role in supporting or countering greenwashing. The findings confirm that AI, when properly implemented and monitored, can promote trust and transparency, but misuse can lead to misleading practices. Recommendations include the need for clear regulations, ethical AI codes, and external audits to ensure responsible AI use in business. © 2025 Malgorzata Wiktoria Paprocka. All rights reserved.},
