	abstract = {As generative AI systems rapidly integrate into our daily lives, the imperative for transparency and explainability has become paramount. This chapter explores the critical role of openness in AI systems, focusing on its importance in mitigating bias, fostering consumer trust, and ensuring ethical AI development. We examine recent policy initiatives, discuss practical implementations of transparency across various industries, and analyze case studies and expert insights. By highlighting the challenges and opportunities in making AI decision-making processes more understandable, we aim to bridge the gap between complex technology and user understanding, paving the way for more responsible, accountable, and trustworthy AI development in the generative era. Through a comprehensive exploration of current practices, emerging technologies, and future directions, this chapter provides a roadmap for achieving transparency in AI systems, ultimately contributing to the development of AI that is not only powerful but also aligned with human values and societal needs. © 2025 Casey Phillips. All rights reserved.},
