	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105009960955?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Department of Library and Information Science, Kwara State University, Malete, Nigeria},
	abstract = {There has been a continuous increase in the adoption and use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in different spheres of life and libraries are not excluded. The pros and benefits of AI have been exhaustively discussed in literature. However, there is limited analysis of the social, economic, and environmental impacts of adopting AI in libraries. Hence, this study analyzed the socio-economic and environmental impacts of Artificial Intelligence adoption in libraries. This chapter adopts the desk review approach to search and gather relevant literature. The study demonstrated that there is a need for up-skilling librarians, managing societal impacts, and ensuring responsible AI adoption to improve library services and address apprehensions about workforce changes. It has been established that adoption of AI in libraries may boost efficiency but there are worries that the technologies may worsen economic inequality and cause disruptions. Also, there are concerns about job displacement and its strategic planning is required to understand the financial advantages of AI deployment in libraries. Furthermore, AI-driven metrics contribute to data-driven decision-making for environmentally responsible library administration by facilitating waste minimization, energy efficiency, and other sustainable library practices. Future studies should examine the specific skills librarians need to effectively integrate AI into library operations and recommend training programs. Also, future studies should address concern about job displacement by exploring strategies for job augmentation and the creation of new roles using AI. © 2025 Walter de Gruyter GmbH. All rights reserved.},
