	abstract = {AI has touched human rights through literature and law, providing modern society both possibilities and challenges. AI has major human rights issues as it spreads. AI in human rights literature and law shows the necessity for flexible legal frameworks to accommodate technology's difficulties. This conversation promotes ethical AI development and proactive human rights protection in an AI-driven world. This paper examines literature and law on human rights and AI's impact on society. It also defines human rights and their value, then trace their history in literature and law. We examine AI and human rights, including its difficulties and prospects for protecting individual rights. Current AI governance legal frameworks have holes and inconsistencies that require legislative revisions. The paper advises govern-ments, technologists, and human rights advocates to integrate human rights into AI research. Finally, it discusses how literature influences public image and AI ethics, promoting communication to protect human rights. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing.},
