	abstract = {The integration of artificial intelligence in arts and design higher education, particularly through tools like ChatGPT and Midjourney, is transforming creative processes by development personalized learning, enhancing workflow efficiency, and enabling fast probe of design options. However, these developments raise critical ethical concerns surrounding student autonomy, data privacy, content bias, and the broader implications of AI-driven misinformation. The rise of deepfakes and fake news further amplifies these concerns by manipulating public perception, eroding trust, and challenging the integrity of digital content. By analyzing case studies of AI in art and design education alongside the societal impact of deepfakes, this chapter underlines the need for a balanced approach that integrates technological innovation with ethical responsibility. It argues that responsible AI adoption requires comprehensive training, interdisciplinary collaboration, and robust frameworks to ensure students develop both technical proficiency and ethical awareness. The chapter critically reflects on the pedagogical challenges and opportunities of AI, emphasizing the importance of equipping students with the ability to harness AI as a creative ally while preserving the essence of human ingenuity in artistic expression. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
