	abstract = {Artificial Intelligence (AI) has emerged as a transformative force within the area of healthcare, heralding a brand-new technology inside the shipping of scientific services and patient care. This paper explores the significant impact of AI technologies on the healthcare ecosystem, delving into key areas such as disease diagnosis, treatment personalization, drug discovery, imaging analysis, and administrative efficiency. We also examine the ethical considerations and privacy challenges associated with the integration of AI in healthcare. The paper highlights AI's role in early disease detection, predictive analytics, and the development of personalized treatment plans, showcasing how it enhances the accuracy and speed of medical imaging analysis. Furthermore, we discuss AI's contribution to telemedicine, remote patient monitoring, and robot-assisted surgery, all of which are revolutionizing patient care delivery. In the context of drug discovery and development, AI-driven algorithms are accelerating the identification of novel therapeutics and improving drug safety monitoring. We explore the potential of natural language processing (NLP) in extracting insights from unstructured clinical data, enabling data-driven decision-making and quality improvement. While AI holds immense promise for the healthcare sector, we address the critical need for ethical guidelines and robust data privacy safeguards. Balancing technological advancements with patient trust and data security is crucial for responsible AI implementation in healthcare. This abstract provides a glimpse into the multifaceted role of AI in healthcare and underscores the need for a thoughtful and ethical approach to harnessing the full potential of AI in revolutionizing the future of medicine. © 2025 Author(s).},
