	abstract = {Integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) into Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) systems offers significant opportunities for enhancing educational outcomes. However, it also presents ethical challenges, especially in developing economies like Malaysia. This paper examines global AI ethics frameworks, including UNESCO's Recommendation on the Ethics of Artificial Intelligence, the European Union's AI Act, and the OECD AI Principles, and evaluates their applicability to Malaysia's TVET sector. Through analysis of documented case studies and existing policies, the paper identifies gaps in current practices and proposes a hybrid governance model tailored to Malaysia's unique context. Recommendations include implementing AI transparency protocols, conducting localised bias audits, and providing capacity-building initiatives for educators. This framework aims to guide the ethical integration of AI in Malaysia's TVET sector and can serve as model for other emerging economies. © 2025 IEEE.},
