	abstract = {Artificial intelligence(AI)has been the defining force of the 21st century, quickly transforming industries, economies, and ways of life. AI’s impact is vast, from identifying rare diseases in hospitals to guiding autonomous vehicles through traffic-congested cities. But its rise brings with it a flood of ethical concerns: How do we make it fair in its judgments? Can it protect our privacy in the face of its insatiable data hunger? And how will it redefine work, elevating it or eroding it? This chapter explores “Responsible AI,” a framework(Figure 3.1)designed to harness AI’s potential while anchoring it in ethical principles. Beyond technical prowess, Responsible AI seeks to foster “decent work” jobs that are productive, paid, secure, and dignified, as championed by the International Labour Organization(ILO). Figure 3.1 offers a visual guide to this interplay of ethics and innovation. Figure 3.1 Responsible AI framework. The diagram depicts the Responsible AI framework, highlighting three main components: Ethical Principles, Workplace Impact, and Regulatory Framework, each linked to specific strategies like Bias Prevention, Reskilling Programs, and Legal Frameworks. These elements collectively aim to achieve ethical AI development, sustainable employment, and social and economic benefits. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Hemachandran K and Raul V. Rodriguez individual chapters, the contributors.},
