	affiliations = {Teerthanker Mahaveer College of Pharmacy, Teerthanker Mahaveer University, UP, Moradabad, India; Maharana Pratap College of Pharmacy, Uttar Pradesh, Mandhana, Kanpur, India},
	abstract = {This section of the book talks about explainable and responsible artificial intelligence (AI) in conjunction with cognitive neurostimulation. This field has an enormous amount of promise in helping improve the comprehension of the brain and enhance our cognitive abilities. To alter neuronal activity and, therefore, cognitive processes, certain parts of the brain may be electrical or magnetism stimulated. The term for it is neural stimulation of cognition. Transparency in decision- making is crucial for AI systems that use neurostimulation techniques; thus, it is a significant accomplishment when these systems can articulate the reasoning behind their findings. We address the fact that knowing this relationship is critical to appreciating how AI-driven neurostimulation therapy options impact different brain areas and how this correlates to enhanced cognitive function. This transparency may increase mutual trust between physicians and researchers, improving the efficacy of therapy. Risk minimization and moral concerns are the two aspects that make up proactive AI. We highlight the need for responsible AI systems that prioritize patient safety, informed consent, and privacy in our exploration of the moral problems raised by cognitive neurostimulation. This chapter indicates that neuroscientists, AI experts, and philosophers of ethics engaged cooperatively to develop ethical standards for the use of AI to perform cognitive neurostimulation. This chapter aims primarily at giving a comprehensive review of the simple methods that may be used to combine the rapidly advancing science of cognitive neurostimulation with morally sound and intelligible AI concepts. © 2025 Scrivener Publishing LLC.},
