	abstract = {This study conducts an in-depth investigation into the performance of artificial intelligence (AI) chips under different computing frameworks, focusing on the adaptation mechanism between computing frameworks and chips, the collaborative efficiency of memory bandwidth and parallel computing, as well as the supporting capability of ecological toolchains for commercial applications. This not only relates to the technical positioning of AI chips but also has a significant impact on the foundation of the independent and controllable development of the AI industry. The research is carried out from three main aspects: first, summarizing the current development status of AI chips and pointing out the challenges they are currently facing; second, designing a heterogeneous AI chip evaluation architecture to construct a comprehensive evaluation system covering multiple computing frameworks; third, combining a multi-dimensional evaluation index system to conduct an in-depth analysis of the performance differences of heterogeneous AI chips in the process of adapting to different computing frameworks, the restrictive factors affecting the collaborative efficiency of memory bandwidth and parallel computing, and the shortcomings and advantages of ecological toolchains in supporting commercial applications. Finally, through conclusions and prospects, it clarifies the key directions that need to be prioritized in the future development of this field, and by constructing a multi-dimensional evaluation system, the research provides empirical evidence for technical optimization and industrial implementation. © 2025 IEEE.},
