	abstract = {Deploying AI solutions responsibly is critical, especially for generative AI applications in consumer-facing industries like banking, healthcare, and other such high-risk domains. Enterprises face significant challenges in mitigating risks associated with AI adoption, including regulatory compliance, model robustness, and ethical considerations. This paper presents findings from developing a risk mitigation platform for enterprise AI, highlighting key challenges and best practices. By formulating a responsible AI framework, leveraging a structured risk assessment approach, and integrating a penalty-based disclosure mechanism, we offer insights that can help organizations better prepare for AI solution deployment. Furthermore, we explore the intersection of technical, ethical, and regulatory challenges that enterprises must navigate while implementing AI-driven solutions. This paper aims to provide a practical approach to balancing the competing priorities of AI performance, compliance, and risk mitigation while ensuring that AI systems align with enterprise goals and societal expectations. The findings presented here are intended to guide enterprises in developing scalable and adaptable AI governance frameworks that remain resilient in the face of rapid technological advancements. © 2025 IEEE.},
