	abstract = {Artificial intelligence (AI) can significantly transform the accounting profession by enhancing efficiency and decision-making capabilities but involves challenges such as bias, data security, privacy and legal liability. However, AI regulations vary globally: the United States of America (USA) maintains a decentralised system, while the People’s Republic of China (PRC) uses a more integrated approach. The lack of clear AI governance regulations presents challenges to companies operating internationally. This chapter aims to conduct a comparative analysis of the frameworks for AI application within specific regions, including the USA, the PRC, Japan, and the European Union (EU). This chapter will examine these frameworks and analyse the regulatory strengths, challenges, and themes that can inform the development of AI frameworks in the accounting sector. This chapter concludes with clear recommendations that underpin global best practices. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Manjit Kour and Daniel P. Schutte; individual chapters, the contributors.},
