	abstract = {This paper is to propose a Responsible AI-Enhanced Labor Market Forecasting System that would aid in the fair and conscious policy making. To mitigate bias in labor market data the system applies fairness-aware preprocessing employing the reweighing technique within the IBM AI Fairness 360 (AIF360). Extraction of features is done in a hybrid method by using mutual information with domain-based knowledge so that it is both statistically significant and has policy implications. The forecast is constructed based on the Causal Forest algorithm that allows getting high-quality predictions and simultaneously takes into account the heterogeneous impact of the policy interventions on the employment indicators. The empirical findings indicate that the suggested system is more accurate, fair, and transparent than the traditional models and is both less discriminating and has a high predictive performance. With AIF360, bias and fairness are monitored continuously and this increases accountability. The study can add a generalizable, ethically agreeable model of implementing AI in labor economics, which is likely to enhance the effectiveness of the public policy and social fairness.  © 2025 IEEE.},
