	abstract = {The paper also presents Global AI-Driven Education Exchange (G-AIDE-X) that acts as a new technical platform to address issues of complexities concerning borderless universities experiencing digital transformation brought to bear by AI through collaborative partnering. Several hi-tech technologies ensure that G-AIDE-X framework is coordinated to facilitate adaptation and the achievement of equal security-based education opportunities across various academic systems across different international environments. The G-AIDE-X methodological cycle comprises five steps that begin with assessment of the institutions and move on to the development of unified educational ontology and then decentralized AI infrastructure and finally block-chain-accreditation and the formation of ethical AI governance. The framework incorporates Deep Q-Network (DQN) decision system which will present a Markov Decision Process (MDP) model of university collaborative environments. The technology allows institutions to tailor their policies in planning learning curricula and resource allocation on a blend of institutional factors and data on student interaction. The DQN agent enhances its capabilities by reinforcing learning functions to maintain continuous adaptation during evolution of cross-border academic operations. Global digital collaboration principles serve as the fundamental base for G-AIDE-X to offer an autonomous framework that obeys worldwide digital governance rules for the creation of higher education systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
