	affiliations = {Higher Polytechnic School - LITA, Alioune Diop University, Dakar, Senegal; Higher Polytechnic School - LITA, University Cheikh Anta Diop of Dakar, Dakar, Senegal; Central School for Open Source Software (EC2LT), Dakar, Senegal; Cheikh Hamidou Kane Digital University (UN-CHK), Dakar, Senegal},
	abstract = {The rapid digital transformation of higher education in sub-Saharan Africa faces persistent challenges of scalability, accessibility, and technological sovereignty. This paper investigates the use of LiveKit, an open-source WebRTC-based infrastructure, to support the Université Numérique Cheikh Hamidou Kane (UN-CHK), which currently serves 73,797 students across 18 Open Digital Spaces. We propose an architecture leveraging the national data center in Diamniadio and the SENUM SA fiber optic backbone to ensure digital sovereignty and resilience. Using Apache JMeter, we conducted performance tests simulating 200 concurrent connections. The results show a 100% success rate, an average response time of 81 ms, and a 0% error rate, demonstrating the robustness and scalability of LiveKit under controlled conditions. These findings position LiveKit as a viable, cost-effective, and sovereign alternative to proprietary videoconferencing platforms. The study contributes to advancing large-scale digital education in Africa by providing empirical evidence on the feasibility of deploying open-source real-time communication systems in national infrastructures.  © 2025 IEEE.},
