	abstract = {The digital world of our days is a perfect breeding ground for the prevalence of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in tourism, and such a revolution can help make tourism more personal, efficient and sustainable. Nevertheless, ensuring the ethical usage of AI is a big challenge, which is accompanied by its potential benefits on the other hand privacy, transparency, fairness, and accountability are the main areas of concern. This knowledge shed light on the necessity of trustworthy AI in the tourism industry as well as the emphasis of responsible implemen- tation. this paper set out the main ideas behind Trustworthy AI in Tourism, which involve notions of transparency, accountability, fairness, reliability, and privacy. Through the evaluation of AI applications in domains of tourism, such as personalized recommendations, customer service, predictive analytics, and familiarization with the destination, the paper demonstrates the moiety of the cases and ethical considerations related to its implementation. The paper examines the methods to make sure the AI devices are reliable and looks into examples from real life and the best practices. Ethical rules, transparency mechanisms and interaction with stakeholders are highlighted as the main approaches, among others. A holistic review of the current situation and future scenarios is the basis for the paper's findings, where the compatibility of human-trustworthy AI is revealed and the development of the tourism industry is promoted. © 2025 IEEE.},
