	affiliations = {Datta Meghe Institute of Higher Education and Research, Faculty of Engineering & Technology, Department of Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning, Sawangi, Maharashtra, Wardha, 442001, India},
	abstract = {In our everyday life depends heavily on Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems that power self-driving cars, healthcare facilities, media services, financial institutions, robot factories and internet technology. AI creates important ethical risks when it intrudes into privacy, puts people at risk and affects their employment. This review article studies how AI affects ethics by examining potential problems with suggested solutions to manage them. This paper shows all current ethical risks of AI technology while providing guidance on building responsible artificial intelligence. This review shows why ethical values need to be part of AI creation and reveals good directions to make AI systems work better with humans and make society thrive. This study works as the starting point for researchers' prevention plans and AI ethics practitioners who need a complete understanding of ethical AI system development and its problems.  © 2025 IEEE.},
