	abstract = {The widespread adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) in education is raising concerns about its impact on ethics, especially at the college level. This study examines how gamification can enhance AI ethics awareness among college students by utilizing a gamified AI chatbot prototype. A total of 152 college students in Indonesia who had used AI tools participated in the study. The study employed a quasi-experimental, one-group pretest-posttest design. The study also uses the AI Ethics Perception Scale (AEPS) to measure any differences after the intervention of the gamified chatbot. Results were analyzed using the Wilcoxon Signed-Rank test, which showed a significant increase in AI ethics awareness across all AEPS variables, with Human Oversight (EHO) showing the highest growth. The Spearman's Rank-Order Correlation test revealed that some octalysis variables, such as Epic Meaning and Calling (GEPC), had a positive impact on ethical understanding. This study highlights the effectiveness of gamification in enhancing knowledge of AI ethics and the importance of an interactive approach in AI ethics education.  © 2025 IEEE.},
