	abstract = {This study conducts a rigorous bibliometric analysis of 81 high-impact documents (2015-2025) at the nexus of Strategic Management, ESG, AI, and Finance, utilizing Scopus, Web of Science, and VOSviewer. It aims to map the intellectual structure, track the conceptual evolution, and identify critical research frontiers. Findings confirm the emergence of the 'Dual Persona of AI,' characterized by a strategic shift from perceiving AI solely as an efficiency tool (Solution Persona) to recognizing it as a critical subject demanding rigorous Algorithmic Governance (Dilemma Persona). Analysis of co-authorship networks reveals China, the US, and the UK as central hubs, while co-citation analysis confirms foundational reliance on Risk Management, Agency, and Stakeholder theories. Keyword co-occurrence mapping pinpoints three thematic clusters and reveals critical Ethical Gaps - specifically concerning algorithmic transparency (Explainability Gap), bias, and the urgent need to integrate non-anthropocentric ethics (Nonhuman Ethical Gap) into corporate governance structures. The study concludes by proposing a structured research agenda to guide future scholarship in managing AI's dual role for sustainable and responsible digital transformation. © 2025 IEEE.},
