	abstract = {The world is progressively adopting Artificial Intelligence (AI) across all sectors to improve productivity, decision-making, and service provision. In Jordan, AI is being investigated in many fields, such as healthcare, education, financial services, and government activities. However, the tendency to rapidly embrace AI technologies presents unique challenges, one of the most serious being failures within the system and the legal accountability of individuals and organizations operationally responsible for the systems within which the mistakes are made. The article intends to identify legal responsibility in case a person or administrative organization is to be blamed for AI application inaccuracies in Jordan, focusing intensely on the social and legal consequences. The analysis emphasizes the country's existing legal documents, the ethical aspects of the application of AI technology, and the comprehensive plan for administrative responsibility. The analysis of the components makes it possible to understand better how Jordan can cope with the problems of AI governance and bear the consequences of malfunctioning AI systems and ethical misconduct at the hands of powerful AI. © 2025 IEEE.},
