	abstract = {This chapter delves into in-depth ethical concerns related to AI: the complications and dilemmas involved in developing and deploying it. First, I discuss founding principles, such as fairness, accountability, and transparency, as well as elaborate on how these principles are applied in different applications of AI. It looks at specific ethical issues-like algorithm bias, the prospects for autonomous decision-making, and the social and political effects of surveillance technologies-and cements its findings with case studies as well as many actual examples that demonstrate how risks and opportunities in AI technologies are manifested throughout various sectors-from healthcare to criminal justice. This chapter will supplement the discussions above by bringing forth the means of connection between technology, philosophy, law, and social sciences that shape the lines of AI ethics. It aims to empower stakeholders in responsibly navigating the changing landscape of AI through actionable insights and frameworks for ethical AI practices, as dialogue calls out for a balance between human rights and societal well-being. © 2025 CRC Press.},
