	affiliations = {Bangor University, United Kingdom; Institute of Commonwealth Studies, United Kingdom; Intel, United States},
	abstract = {As General-Purpose Artificial Intelligence (GPAI) systems increasingly function as empathic partners, personal assistants, co-pilots, and companions, the ethical implications of emulated empathy become critical. IEEE P7014.1 establishes a Recommended Practice (RP) to guide the responsible design, deployment, and governance of empathic AI partners. This paper introduces the scope, core ethical concerns, and key recommendations of IEEE P7014.1, emphasizing its role in preventing deception, protecting user autonomy, and ensuring culturally sensitive, bias-aware AI interactions. We highlight how this standard fills a critical gap in AI ethics by focusing on downstream human-AI partnerships and provide actionable insights for researchers, developers, and policymakers to adopt its principles. The goal is to foster global awareness and accelerate the integration of P7014.1 into AI development frameworks.  © 2025 IEEE.},
