	abstract = {The rapid pace of development in Artificial Intelligence (AI) necessitates formulating effective national strategies for its maximization and minimizing its accompanying repercussions. In this article, a proposed National Artificial Intelligence Strategy for Jordan is formulated, with an orientation towards a systemic and organized national structure relevant to Jordan's socio-economic environment. What is new in this proposed National AI Strategy is its localized orientation, blending AI-facilitated economic development, governance, and ethics relevant to Jordan. It also formulates a governance model, with coordination between principal entities such as government, academia, and private sectors, for effective implementation. The proposed strategy sets specific digital transformation targets, in consonance with Jordan's Vision 2030 and National Strategy for Digital Transformation (2021-2025). AI use in critical sectors such as national security, energy, healthcare, and education takes a top position, with a view towards adhering to regulations, utilizing AI in an ethical manner, and developing technology in a sustainable manner. Outcomes include enhancing AI literacy, diversifying economies, enhancing employment in AI-related industries, and national competitiveness at a global level. This work forms part of an emerging portfolio of studies in national AI strategies and sets a country-specific model in consonance with Jordan's specific development aims, offering a model for AI strategy development in emerging economies.  © 2025 IEEE.},
