	affiliations = {National University, School of Accountancy, Business and Management, NU Lipa, Philippines; National University, Senior High School, NU Lipa, Philippines; National University, School of Architecture, Computing and Engineering, NU Lipa, Philippines},
	abstract = {There are benefits and drawbacks to the growing use of artificial intelligence (AI) systems in education, especially concerning academic integrity. The ethical application of AI tools is still poorly understood in the sector of education, where critical thinking and creativity are essential. This study focuses on AI as a useful tool and a possible concern by examining how teachers and students view its role in academic integrity. Semi-structured interviews were conducted among 30 students and faculty members, and themes were identified through thematic analysis. The results showed that people believe AI tools may boost productivity, improve research results, and foster innovation. Concerns about plagiarism, over-reliance, and a lack of critical thinking draw attention to the dangers of abuse based on the result. To encourage responsible AI use, the study emphasizes the significance of explicit institutional standards, ethical education, and assessment changes. Practical implications were derived from striking a balance between innovation and integrity in the realm of education, this study adds to the expanding corpus of information on AI ethics in academia. It suggests creating thorough regulations and educational initiatives to guarantee that AI tools raise academic standards rather than lower them. © 2025 IEEE.},
