	affiliations = {Kasetsart University Sriracha, Computer Science and Information Technology Department, Siracha, Chonburi, 20230, Thailand},
	abstract = {Global labor markets are changing because of the rapid adoption of artificial intelligence (AI), which is replacing regular activities and opening up new opportunities. The need for strong technical and analytical abilities is growing as more businesses incorporate AI into business operations, especially in areas such as machine learning, deep learning, natural language processing, cloud computing, and AI ethics. Determining the most in-demand AI talents requires finding discrepancies between the supply of workers and employer demands, and highlighting reskilling and upskilling goals. To this end, we applied AI-driven text analytics to job advertisements, labor market information, and industry reports. The results highlight the urgent need for workforce solutions by exposing serious mismatches in domains including deep learning, natural language processing, and responsible AI. This report presents a framework for creating flexible policies that improve workforce preparedness in an AI-driven economy, thereby providing evidence-based insights for decision-makers in government, education, and business. © 2025 IEEE.},
