	abstract = {As humanity crosses critical ecological thresholds while rapidly advancing high technologies such as artificial intelligence (AI), quantum computing, and space systems, a new paradigm of technology governance is urgently needed, one that respects the planet as a living system with intrinsic rights and priorities. This paper introduces a value-based governance framework that integrates five foundational principles—dignity, identity, inclusion, trust, and agency—as ethical considerations to guide AI innovation. Framed within the vision of the planet as a living system, the approach expands traditional AI ethics by embedding planetary consciousness and long-term ecological stewardship into the core of AI development and deployment. Going beyond sustainability metrics, the framework offers a value-sensitive approach that centers both human well-being and planetary integrity. By examining practical cases—from energy-hungry AI data centers to extractive digital infrastructure—the paper demonstrates how technology decisions can be reframed through ecological ethics, planetary inclusion, and intergenerational accountability. It also discusses how the framework complements and strengthens existing global efforts such as the UN SDGs, ESG standards, and planetary boundaries. The paper concludes with recommendations for policy, standards, and innovation ecosystems to align emerging technologies with the rights of nature and the dignity of all life. ©20XX IEEE.},
