	abstract = {Australia has adopted a cautious and deliberative approach to regulation of the implementation and use of artificial intelligence technologies, and at the end of 2024, no AI-specific legislation has been proposed, let alone implemented. The Federal Government of Australia has consulted with the community about legislative and regulatory approaches that balance economic development and innovation against the need to ensure responsible and safe use of AI. Through these consultation processes the Government has developed some proposed ‘mandatory guardrails’ for high-risk AI, as well as some voluntary AI ethics principles that are aligned with the proposed mandatory guardrails. Some of the mandatory guardrails may be legislated in an AI-specific law; however, it is likely that some regulation of AI will be implemented through amendments to existing laws © The Editors and Contributors Severally 2025. All rights reserved.},
